      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "3. Find the right skill — don't improvise",
      "prov:value": "This section used to list three directory paths instead. That is the practice\n`AGENTS.md` opens by warning against — *\"hardcoding a path is how a skill goes\nmissing the moment the layout moves\"* — and one of the three names a graph typology\nthat has since been renamed. The declaration is the answer; a path is a\nsnapshot of it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/guides/agent-onboarding.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "9. Where to look things up",
      "prov:value": "| Question | Answer |\n|---|---|\n| Project commands, conventions | `AGENTS.md` (the agent-generic source of truth) |\n| What a skill does | `skills/**/`, or the generated [instruction bodies]({{ site.baseurl }}/reference/skill-instructions/) |\n| A skill's typed contract | [Skill schema reference]({{ site.baseurl }}/reference/skills/) |\n| What a QA criterion means | `content/pipeline/qa-criteria-registry.ts` — descriptions are the spec |\n| The block schema | `schemas/types.ts` |\n| The QA sidecar schema | `schemas/block-qa.ts` |\n| What this environment can do | `cat-harness/scenarios/capabilities/*.json`, `--check-deps` |\n| Lean tooling roadmap | [Lean tooling proposal](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/198) |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#198"
      ]
    }
  ]
